---
import Layers from "./Layers.astro";

const stats = [
  { num: "26.0k", unit: "", label: "tokens, median, in context before the first reply" },
  { num: "70", unit: "%", label: "of all tokens processed went to that starting load" },
  { num: "9", unit: "/12", label: "skills listed in every session and never once used" },
];
---

<section class="problem" id="problem">
  <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
  <h2>The layers pile up, and you never see them.</h2>
  <p class="section-lede">
    Each layer is added by a different tool, plugin or file, and the harness resends all of it on
    every turn. None of it shows up anywhere you can see. A bloated context is one reason agents go
    off the rails: when one drifts, you can't tell whether it was missing something or buried under
    it.
  </p>
  <ol class="turns" aria-label="The same stack, resent on every turn">
    {
      ["Turn 1", "Turn 2", "Turn 3"].map((turn) => (
        <li>
          <Layers />
          <span>{turn}</span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>
  <dl class="stats">
    {
      stats.map((s) => (
        <div class="stat">
          <dt>
            {s.num}
            <small>{s.unit}</small>
          </dt>
          <dd>{s.label}</dd>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </dl>
  <p class="footnote">Figures from the demo history behind every sample on this page.</p>
</section>
